---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

const title = 'The Jack Maguire Compatibility Quiz';
const description = 'A short, behavior-based compatibility quiz for people curious about dating Jack Maguire.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="compatibility-page">
			<section class="quiz-hero">
				<h1>Would you and Jack get along?</h1>
				<p class="hero-copy">This is a compatibility quiz, not a personality test. It asks how you handle teasing, uncertainty, quiet, curiosity, and the occasional over-planned walk through New York.</p>
				<div class="hero-note"><strong>How it works</strong><span>16 questions · about 4 minutes · no email required</span></div>
			</section>

			<section class="quiz-shell" aria-labelledby="quiz-title">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<h2 id="quiz-title">Choose the answer that feels most like you.</h2>
					<p>Most options describe a healthy relationship. Choose what you would actually enjoy, not what sounds most admirable.</p>
				</div>
				<form id="compatibility-form">
					<div id="question-list"></div>
					<button class="submit-button" type="submit">Show my compatibility report <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
				</form>
				<p class="form-note">Your answers stay in this browser. They are used to make the report below and are not sent anywhere.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="report" class="report-section" hidden aria-live="polite"></section>

			<section class="wiki-section" id="matchmaker-wiki">
				<div class="section-heading">
					<h2>What Jack is looking for</h2>
					<p>These notes describe the difference between a person who looks good on paper and a person Jack wants to keep seeing.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="wiki-grid">
					<article class="wiki-card wide"><h3>Core match profile</h3><p>A strong match will usually have most of these qualities:</p><ol><li><strong>Sharp, warm humor.</strong> She can tease and be teased, handle irreverent or slightly dark jokes, make callbacks, and give as good as she gets.</li><li><strong>Direct communication.</strong> She says uncomfortable things plainly and can say “you’re being mean right now” without cruelty.</li><li><strong>Emotional strength with softness.</strong> She has boundaries without becoming cold and can be tender without collapsing.</li><li><strong>Attention to detail.</strong> She remembers specific moments, preferences, sounds, routines, and phrases. Generic attentiveness is not enough.</li><li><strong>A different point of view.</strong> Her background, discipline, culture, or life path expands Jack’s default frame and gives the relationship its own references.</li><li><strong>Not easily impressed.</strong> She is not awed by ambition, competence, money, intelligence, or dominance. She can lovingly roll her eyes.</li><li><strong>Warm ties to family or chosen family.</strong> She has close relationships and makes integration feel normal.</li><li><strong>Good ordinary life.</strong> A couch evening, simple meal, walk, or shared routine feels good.</li><li><strong>Accountability with context.</strong> She can see anxiety underneath sharp or controlling stress behavior while still naming the behavior clearly.</li><li><strong>Intellectual range.</strong> She wants to talk about ideas, from psychology and cities to economics, technology, culture, philosophy, media, or whatever is interesting that day.</li></ol></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Current non-negotiables</h3><ul><li>Sweet to Jack</li><li>Really sharp</li><li>Close with friends and/or family</li><li>Comfortable taking things slowly</li><li>Able to genuinely enjoy relaxing</li><li>Sincerely curious about Jack and his life</li><li>Direct enough to reduce ambiguity</li><li>Emotionally brave in hard conversations</li><li>Capable of playful banter</li><li>Someone Jack is excited to see again</li></ul><p class="small-note">There is no height requirement. The quiz asks separately whether someone is comfortable dating a guy under 5'5", because attraction and practical fit still deserve an honest answer.</p></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Attraction rule</h3><p>Paper fit cannot carry the match. Jack has to feel real pull and want to see her again. “She seems perfect” is not the same as “I am excited to see her.”</p><h3 class="subhead">Nice, but not core</h3><p>Hot, dresses well, socially polished, and conventionally impressive can help. They should never drive selection.</p></article>
					<article class="wiki-card wide"><h3>Early screening criteria</h3><div class="signal-grid"><div><h4>Humor</h4><p class="good">Strong: natural teasing, callbacks, escalation, light roasting, reciprocal play.</p><p class="weak">Weak: polite laughter, brittle reactions, performance instead of play, or deference.</p></div><div><h4>Directness</h4><p class="good">Strong: clear answers, stated preferences, disagreement without drama, named discomfort.</p><p class="weak">Weak: hints, “I’m fine” when she is not, passive aggression, or making Jack chase clarity.</p></div><div><h4>Curiosity</h4><p class="good">Strong: specific follow-ups, remembered details, interest in work, routines, friends, tastes, and ideas.</p><p class="weak">Weak: generic questions, surface conversation, or enjoying pursuit without investigating him back.</p></div><div><h4>Relaxation</h4><p class="good">Strong: a walk, quiet bar, meal, couch, or unplanned moment can be enough.</p><p class="weak">Weak: restlessness with ordinary intimacy, constant phone checking, or needing every plan to be novel.</p></div></div></article>
					<article class="wiki-card wide"><h3>The relationship dynamic</h3><div class="two-column"><div><h4>Emotional experience</h4><ul><li>Clear mutual choosing</li><li>Physical closeness that is sexual and tender</li><li>Safety for honesty</li><li>Shared values and mutual effort</li><li>Long-horizon commitment</li><li>Care that does not require performance</li><li>A feeling of being on the same team</li></ul></div><div><h4>Daily texture</h4><ul><li>Playful, competitive banter</li><li>Shared walks and neighborhood plans</li><li>Small rituals and private language</li><li>Cooking, shows, food, and drink</li><li>Integration with friends and family</li><li>Quiet domestic moments that feel chosen</li></ul></div></div><p>Jack expresses love by building specific shared experiences: a walk-to-bar-to-food arc, a place with atmosphere, a neighborhood, a recurring reference, or a domestic evening that feels intentional. A strong match receives this as romantic rather than excessive management.</p></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Matchmaker operating rules</h3><ol><li>Do not overweight paper fit.</li><li>Treat banter as diagnostic.</li><li>Keep directness non-negotiable.</li><li>Look for sweetness with strength.</li><li>Avoid hot-but-empty matches.</li><li>Be cautious with traveler or temporary fantasy dynamics.</li><li>Favor slow-building intimacy.</li></ol></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Risk patterns</h3><ul><li><strong>Ambiguity intolerance:</strong> prefer naturally clear partners.</li><li><strong>Over-functioning:</strong> favor mutual initiative and load-carrying.</li><li><strong>Constraint-amplified intensity:</strong> test ordinary, available, low-drama conditions.</li><li><strong>Stability aversion:</strong> use gradual commitment and explicit pacing.</li><li><strong>Relationship blitz:</strong> avoid going from independence to constant togetherness without a ramp.</li><li><strong>Fantasy maintenance:</strong> prioritize viable, present, emotionally available candidates.</li></ul></article>
					<article class="wiki-card wide"><h3>Date design instructions</h3><p><strong>Best format:</strong> a walk, an atmospheric drink or coffee, optional food if chemistry is strong, and an easy exit.</p><p><strong>Good ingredients:</strong> a neighborhood, bookstore, market, park, waterfront, unusual street, specific food stop, and room for a detour.</p><p><strong>Avoid:</strong> static dinner-only dates, formal settings, loud venues, generic drinks with no surrounding texture, errands, or premature couple-like intensity.</p><p><strong>Observe:</strong> Does she tease him? Ask real questions? Notice things? Enjoy wandering? Make the ordinary better? Does Jack relax? Does he want to make out? Does he want to see her again without arguing himself into it?</p></article>
					<article class="wiki-card wide scorecard"><h3>Candidate evaluation scorecard</h3><p>Rate each category from 1 to 5 after a date, based on observed behavior rather than projected potential.</p><div class="score-list"><span>Humor and banter</span><span>Direct communication</span><span>Emotional strength and softness</span><span>Attention to detail</span><span>Curiosity about Jack</span><span>Intellectual depth and range</span><span>Friends and family ecosystem</span><span>Ordinary-life potential</span><span>Independent world of her own</span><span>Pacing and availability</span><span>Reciprocal effort</span><span>Physical and romantic pull</span></div><p class="small-note"><strong>4.5 to 5.0:</strong> strong match. <strong>3.8 to 4.4:</strong> explore if attraction is real. <strong>3.0 to 3.7:</strong> continue only with clear chemistry and unusually strong signals. <strong>Below 3.0:</strong> deprioritize. Any score without real attraction does not advance.</p></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Red flags</h3><ul><li>Indirect communication or emotional punishment</li><li>Fragility around teasing</li><li>Excessive deference</li><li>Lack of curiosity about Jack</li><li>Status attraction without engagement</li><li>Constant need for stimulation</li><li>High attraction with low viability</li><li>Fast pressure for intense commitment</li><li>Passive receipt of effort</li><li>Ambiguity used as control</li></ul></article>
					<article class="wiki-card"><h3>Green flags</h3><ul><li>Warm teasing early</li><li>Pushback without coldness</li><li>Specific questions and remembered details</li><li>A real world of her own</li><li>Loyalty and integrity</li><li>Ideas, affection, and clear boundaries</li><li>Slow development without avoidance</li><li>Feeling challenged and cared for</li><li>Excitement that feels calm and joyful</li></ul></article>
					<article class="wiki-card wide final-rule"><h3>Final match decision</h3><p>A match is viable only when all four conditions are present:</p><div class="four-rules"><strong>1. Real attraction</strong><strong>2. Reciprocal humor</strong><strong>3. Clear communication</strong><strong>4. Good ordinary life</strong></div><p>If one is missing, proceed cautiously. If two or more are missing, do not advance the match.</p></article>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<script>
	type Question = { id: string; category: string; text: string; options: string[]; scores: number[] };
	const questions: Question[] = [
		{ id: 'banter', category: 'Banter', text: 'A person you are dating teases you about one of your habits. Which response sounds most natural?', options: ['Smile and explain the habit. I prefer jokes that do not put either person on the spot.', 'Tease them back and bring the joke up again later.', 'Laugh and move on. I enjoy warmth more than verbal sparring.', 'Say whether it landed, then keep the mood easy.'], scores: [2, 4, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'conflict', category: 'Clarity', text: 'You leave a date unsure whether one comment bothered you. What would you usually do next?', options: ['Sleep on it and mention it only if it still matters the next day.', 'Talk it through with a friend before deciding whether to raise it.', 'See whether the same thing happens again before treating it as a problem.', 'Tell the person which comment stayed with you and ask what they meant.'], scores: [2, 2, 2, 4] },
		{ id: 'quiet', category: 'Ordinary life', text: 'You and your partner have a free Saturday with no plans. Which day sounds best?', options: ['Walk around the neighborhood, buy something for dinner, and spend the rest of the day at home.', 'Handle separate errands or projects, then meet for dinner.', 'Find a concert, exhibit, or neighborhood event that neither of you has tried.', 'Pick a useful project and work on it together.'], scores: [4, 2, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'curiosity', category: 'Curiosity', text: 'Someone tells you about work or an interest you know little about. How do you tend to respond?', options: ['Ask practical questions until you understand what their day is like.', 'Share a similar experience so the conversation has common ground.', 'Pick one detail that interests you and keep asking about it.', 'Listen closely and let them decide how much they want to explain.'], scores: [2, 2, 4, 2] },
		{ id: 'detail', category: 'Attention', text: 'Which gesture makes you feel most cared for?', options: ['Taking an annoying task off my plate when I am busy.', 'Planning a surprise that took real effort.', 'Saying plainly what they appreciate about me.', 'Remembering an offhand preference and using it weeks later.'], scores: [2, 2, 2, 4] },
		{ id: 'pace', category: 'Pacing', text: 'The first month is going well. What amount of contact would you prefer?', options: ['Text throughout the day and spend most free evenings together.', 'Make clear plans and show affection while both people keep their normal routines.', 'Go on a few dates each week but keep texting fairly light.', 'Spend a lot of time together early, then adjust if either person needs more room.'], scores: [2, 4, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'independence', category: 'Independence', text: 'When a relationship becomes serious, what should remain separate?', options: ['Friendships should remain separate, while most other parts of life combine.', 'Each person should keep some hobbies and time alone.', 'Both people should keep a full life and deliberately set aside regular time together.', 'Most free time should become shared, with either person able to ask for space.'], scores: [2, 2, 4, 2] },
		{ id: 'ideas', category: 'Depth', text: 'Which long conversation would you most want to have with a partner?', options: ['An argument about why people, cities, technology, or culture work the way they do.', 'A conversation about personal history and how it shaped both of you.', 'A practical conversation about the life you want to build.', 'A night of funny stories, gossip, and cultural references.'], scores: [4, 2, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'family', category: 'Community', text: 'How involved should a partner become with your friends or family?', options: ['The relationships can stay mostly separate as long as everyone is respectful.', 'A partner should gradually become a real part of that world.', 'The couple should build a new shared social circle while each person keeps older ties.', 'It should depend on the people involved rather than follow a fixed expectation.'], scores: [2, 4, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'effort', category: 'Reciprocity', text: 'One person plans a thoughtful date. What should the balance look like over time?', options: ['The person who enjoys planning can keep doing it, while the other shows clear appreciation.', 'The couple should alternate turns so the work stays even.', 'The other person should notice what made it thoughtful and plan something equally specific next.', 'Plans should stay mostly spontaneous, with both people deciding in the moment.'], scores: [2, 2, 4, 2] },
		{ id: 'accountability', category: 'Emotional strength', text: 'During a stressful night, your partner says your tone has become sharp. What response feels most like you?', options: ['Ask what landed badly, own the tone, and explain the stress after that.', 'Take a break and return to the conversation later that evening.', 'Apologize and repair the mood, then discuss the cause another time.', 'Explain the pressure and agree on a phrase either person can use before the tone gets worse.'], scores: [4, 2, 2, 2] },
		{ id: 'stimulation', category: 'Ordinary life', text: 'Which kind of shared week sounds best?', options: ['Two busy independent lives with one date both people look forward to.', 'Several social plans and at least one new place to try.', 'Time spent working toward a shared goal or project.', 'A few routine nights together, a walk or meal, and one planned outing.'], scores: [2, 2, 2, 4] },
		{ id: 'unimpressed', category: 'Independence', text: 'You are dating someone unusually accomplished. How would you show interest?', options: ['Ask about the work and celebrate the wins with them.', 'Let them lead when the subject is in their area of expertise.', 'Stay curious, disagree when you do, and tease them as freely as anyone else.', 'Focus mostly on the parts of their life that have nothing to do with achievement.'], scores: [2, 2, 4, 2] },
		{ id: 'height', category: 'Practical fit', text: 'How would you feel about dating a guy who is under 5\'5\"?', options: ['I usually prefer taller men, but chemistry could outweigh that preference.', 'Height has very little effect on whether I find someone attractive.', 'I could date him, though the height difference might stay on my mind.', 'I know I would not be attracted, so I would rather be honest about it.'], scores: [2, 4, 2, 0] },
		{ id: 'pull', category: 'Attraction', text: 'After a first date, what is the strongest reason to say yes to a second?', options: ['Our values and the direction of our lives seem compatible.', 'The conversation was easy and I noticed no serious concerns.', 'They were thoughtful, kind, and clearly interested.', 'I found myself wanting more time with them and more physical closeness.'], scores: [2, 2, 2, 4] },
		{ id: 'desire', category: 'Attraction', text: 'Three months into a relationship, which sign would matter most to you?', options: ['An ordinary evening together is something I want to repeat.', 'We can disagree without either person becoming cruel or shutting down.', 'We support each other’s goals and can make plans for the future.', 'Our friends and routines fit together without much friction.'], scores: [4, 2, 2, 2] },
	];

	const list = document.querySelector('#question-list');
	const form = document.querySelector('#compatibility-form') as HTMLFormElement;
	const report = document.querySelector('#report') as HTMLElement;
	if (list) {
		list.innerHTML = questions.map((q, index) => `<fieldset class="question-card"><legend><span>${String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>${q.text}</legend><div class="answer-grid">${q.options.map((option, optionIndex) => `<label><input type="radio" name="${q.id}" value="${optionIndex}" required><span class="answer-option"><span class="answer-control" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="answer-copy">${option}</span></span></label>`).join('')}</div></fieldset>`).join('');
	}

	form?.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
		event.preventDefault();
		const data = new FormData(form);
		const scores = questions.map((q) => q.scores[Number(data.get(q.id))]);
		const total = scores.reduce((sum, score) => sum + score, 0);
		const percent = Math.round((total / (questions.length * 4)) * 100);
		const categoryScores = questions.reduce((acc, q, index) => {
			acc[q.category] ??= [];
			acc[q.category].push(scores[index]);
			return acc;
		}, {} as Record<string, number[]>);
		const categoryMarkup = Object.entries(categoryScores).map(([category, values]) => {
			const value = Math.round((values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / (values.length * 4)) * 100);
			return `<div class="result-row"><span>${category}</span><div class="bar"><i style="width:${value}%"></i></div><strong>${value}%</strong></div>`;
		}).join('');
		const verdict = percent >= 82 ? ['Strong possibility', 'Your preferences match Jack’s on most of the situations in this quiz. A date would still need to answer two questions the quiz cannot: do you enjoy each other’s humor, and is there mutual attraction?'] : percent >= 69 ? ['Worth a real date', 'You prefer the same relationship style as Jack in several areas, with some differences in how you would spend time or handle closeness.'] : percent >= 56 ? ['Mixed fit', 'Your answers describe a healthy relationship, but several of your preferences differ from Jack’s. A strong in-person connection would have to do more of the work.'] : ['Probably not a match', 'Your answers describe a reasonable way to date, but it is different from the relationship Jack wants. The score is about fit with one person, not relationship quality.'];
		report.hidden = false;
		report.innerHTML = `<div class="report-inner"><div class="report-head"><div><h2>${verdict[0]}</h2><p>${verdict[1]}</p></div><div class="score-number"><strong>${percent}</strong><span>Jack fit score</span></div></div><div class="category-results"><h3>What shaped the result</h3>${categoryMarkup}</div><div class="report-callout"><strong>What the score cannot test</strong><p>Jack also needs mutual attraction, reciprocal humor, clear communication, and ordinary time that both people enjoy. A quiz can test stated preferences. It cannot tell whether two people want another date.</p></div><a class="report-link" href="#matchmaker-wiki">Read the full matchmaker wiki <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>`;
		report.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
	});
</script>

<style>
	:global(body) { background: #f7f6f1; color: #1c1d1b; }
	.compatibility-page { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) 7rem; }
	.quiz-hero { max-width: 900px; padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7rem) 0 clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5rem); }
	.compatibility-page h1, .compatibility-page h2, .compatibility-page h3, .compatibility-page h4 { font-family: var(--font-heading); letter-spacing: -.035em; }
	.quiz-hero h1 { max-width: 850px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 8vw, 6rem); line-height: .93; text-wrap: balance; }
	.hero-copy { max-width: 68ch; margin: 1.75rem 0 0; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	.hero-note { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #bfc3b5; font-size: .86rem; }
	.hero-note span { color: #6c6e66; }
	.quiz-shell, .report-inner { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #cfd2c7; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3.75rem); }
	.section-heading { max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
	.section-heading h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem); line-height: .98; }
	.section-heading p:last-child { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: #666961; line-height: 1.6; }
	:global(.question-card) { margin: 0; padding: 2rem 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e0e1da; }
	:global(.question-card legend) { width: 100%; padding: 0 0 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; }
	:global(.question-card legend span) { display: inline-block; width: 2rem; color: #9ba08c; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .08em; vertical-align: .18em; }
	:global(.answer-grid) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .7rem; }
	:global(.answer-grid label) { display: flex; min-height: 68px; cursor: pointer; }
	:global(.answer-grid input) { position: absolute; opacity: 0; }
	:global(.answer-grid label span) { width: 100%; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid #d9dbd2; color: #52554c; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.4; transition: .15s ease; }
	:global(.answer-grid label:hover span), :global(.answer-grid input:focus-visible + span) { border-color: #69713b; }
	:global(.answer-grid input:checked + span) { border-color: #69713b; background: #eef0e5; color: #24261f; box-shadow: inset 4px 0 #69713b; }
	.submit-button { min-height: 52px; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border: 0; background: #1c1d1b; color: #fff; cursor: pointer; font: 700 .95rem var(--font-heading); transition: background-color .16s ease, color .16s ease; }
	.submit-button span, .report-link span { margin-left: 1.5rem; }
	.submit-button:hover { background: #69713b; }
	.form-note, .small-note { color: #777a70; font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.form-note { margin: 1rem 0 0; }
	:global(.report-section) { padding: 4rem 0 0; scroll-margin-top: 1rem; }
	:global(.report-inner) { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #dcded6; padding: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); }
	:global(.report-head) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; align-items: flex-start; }
	:global(.report-head h2) { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 5rem); line-height: .9; }
	:global(.report-head p) { max-width: 650px; color: #5f6259; line-height: 1.6; }
	:global(.score-number) { min-width: 130px; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #d9dbd2; text-align: center; }
	:global(.score-number strong) { display: block; font: 700 3.5rem/.9 var(--font-heading); }
	:global(.score-number span) { display: block; margin-top: .5rem; color: #69713b; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	:global(.category-results) { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #dcded6; }
	:global(.category-results h3) { margin: 0 0 1.3rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }
	:global(.result-row) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr 48px; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin: .85rem 0; font-size: .88rem; }
	:global(.result-row strong) { text-align: right; }
	:global(.bar) { height: 8px; background: #e8e9e1; }
	:global(.bar i) { display: block; height: 100%; background: #9da56f; }
	:global(.report-callout) { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding: 1.25rem; background: #eef0e5; }
	:global(.report-callout p) { margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 1.55; }
	:global(.report-link) { display: inline-block; margin-top: 2rem; color: #454c25; font-weight: 700; }
	.wiki-section { padding-top: clamp(6rem, 12vw, 10rem); }
	.wiki-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem) clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
	.wiki-card { min-width: 0; padding: 1.5rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid #9fa58d; background: transparent; }
	.wiki-card.wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
	.wiki-card h3 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.6rem; }
	.wiki-card h4 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
	.wiki-card p, .wiki-card li { max-width: 72ch; color: #565a50; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	.wiki-card ol, .wiki-card ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
	.wiki-card li { margin: .45rem 0; }
	.wiki-card strong { color: #292b25; }
	.subhead { margin-top: 2rem !important; }
	.signal-grid, .two-column { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem 2rem; }
	.signal-grid > div { padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #dcded6; }
	.signal-grid p { margin: .45rem 0 0; }
	.signal-grid .good::before { content: 'Strong  '; color: #69713b; font-weight: 800; }
	.signal-grid .weak::before { content: 'Weak  '; color: #9b6d50; font-weight: 800; }
	.score-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #d7d9d0; }
	.score-list span { padding: .8rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #d7d9d0; color: #55594e; font-size: .84rem; }
